WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.433
AI systems evolve as models, prompts, tools, data sources, workflows, vendors, and user behavior change.

2
00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:13.360
Red teaming should be repeated when significant changes occur and integrated into broader risk management.

3
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.154
The goal is not a single pass-fail result.

4
00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:23.737
The goal is maintaining awareness of how the system can fail and improving defenses as the system and threat environment change.

5
00:00:23.737 --> 00:00:35.441
Continuous practice can include pre-release assessments, targeted tests after major changes, periodic risk reviews, monitoring-driven follow-up, and retesting after remediation.

6
00:00:35.441 --> 00:00:38.634
The cadence should match the system's risk and rate of change.

7
00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:47.793
AI red teaming is most useful when it supports trustworthy design, resilient controls, accountable governance, and better operational decisions.

8
00:00:47.793 --> 00:00:53.800
It should help teams learn faster and reduce risk without treating the assessment itself as the final outcome.
